{"agent":"fleet-fixes-n","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`left_text` decides the wording purely from the sign of `remaining_s` and hard-codes \"in its grace period\" for *every* negative value, even though `Lease` has no knowledge of `grace_s`. Given a lease with `ttl_s=60`, `renewed_at=t`, `now = t + 60 + grace_s + 100` (a lease that has been dead for over a minute past the end of its grace), the method returns `\"ran out 160s ago, in its grace period\"`. That is factually false: `state.active_leases(now, grace_s)` no longer contains this lease, the file is claimable, and with a configured `grace_s=0` there is no grace at all, yet the text still asserts one. The previous code (\"(-160s left)\") was ugly but at least did not claim liveness that does not exist. In `reporting.py` the new call renders `it.lease` for an item that carries one (the shown block has no liveness predicate), so `ddflow show` on a long-expired lease now prints \"(ran out Ns ago, in its grace period)\" and tells the operator the opposite of the truth — the file is free. `left_text` needs the grace window (or a liveness flag) to distinguish \"past TTL, still live\" from \"expired\", and the test only ever exercises the in-grace case, so this branch is untested.","digest":"ac902d1bd1559bee","location":"ddflow/core/records.py:175 (`Lease.left_text`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/records.py:175 (`Lease.left_text`)"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The test's name and the stated intent (\"then ddflow next / ddflow show\") promise coverage of the `show` surface, but the test never invokes `show`: it calls `left_text` directly and drives `schedule.item_blocker` in-process. The `reporting.py` edit is therefore wired only by the helper's own unit assertion; a defect in that call site (wrong argument, missed `time.time()`, formatting change) would still leave the suite green. Add an actual `run_cli(repo, \"show\")` (at `late`) and assert the output contains no `-` countdown and no `for another -`, so the surface claimed by the bug report is really covered.","digest":"5e9f1e22483f7a44","location":"tests/test_lease_grace_countdown.py:15 (`test_plan_and_show_never_print_a_negative_countdown`)","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_lease_grace_countdown.py:15 (`test_plan_and_show_never_print_a_negative_countdown`)"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":3598,"diff_sha":"ec3f394d6292c9118791349222eba7f402e7d0cd613d00726b1bc833eb293394","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":67.2,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"2ce3464b2fbbb7df","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Ba3425a7aa8.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261017T233455Z-2b707e01.jsonl","reason":"","review_id":"a6549d24d934","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"83acb28f7924de18a0fdc7d18558a51793c14908","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/core/records.py:175 (`Lease.left_text`)","tests/test_lease_grace_countdown.py:15 (`test_plan_and_show_never_print_a_negative_countdown`)"],"tree_sha":"83acb28f7924+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e9fd43c2b4b08f297e5c264f7","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":77451,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-Ba3425a7aa8","ts":"2026-10-17T23:36:02.406727Z"}
